B)	Lots of proposed fixes for this
C)	Lots of proposed fixes for this
D)	Fixing the levels and the goals would help this, I think.

1) Take the fight to the enemy (A, D):  Make the top tier of demons (Marili=
ths, Balors, Pit Fiends) more dangerous, fewer in number, and more aggressi=
ve during the assention run (teleport in to attack you at while you try to =
escape?), then improved extinction/generation handling code (minimally, rec=
ord DEATHS rather than BIRTHS, perhaps make it so it keeps track of individ=
uals?)  The player now has incentive to track down and slay these demons on=
e by one, prior to the assention run.
Coding difficulty:  Easy to implement in a minimal way: Easy to punch up th=
e difficulty of the monsters (ac, speed, damage output, and choice of spell=
s!), Easy to make existing ones teleport to meet you once you have the amul=
et (piggyback on the covetous monster code + u.demigod), Easy to dial back =
the number required for extinction.  Harder, I think, to improve the code s=
o that individuals can move across levels.

2) Multiple partial adventurer kits (E): You aren't the only one who's trie=
d to raid gehennom, make treasure troves of loot that reflect this.  The st=
and-alone form of this would probably be a new type of grave. This concentr=
ates the loot into one spot, so you can get several of those alchemy reagen=
ts at once, and have an increased chance at the rarer ones. Minimal improve=
ments to the pet code would probably be good, at least enough so that you c=
an take their equipment and hand them things (which they may subsequently d=
rop, as per existing code). More spare magic items means more incentive to =
manage your pets weapons and armor.
Coding difficulty:  The level generation code is like kryptonite to me.

3) Competing adventurers (E, F):  You aren't even the only one who's trying=
 to raid gehennom RIGHT NOW.  Make player monsters to carry the loot from 2=
.  These player monsters would have more items available to them, and offer=
 the somewhat unusual problem of how to kill them without them wasting good=
 consumables, especially as their gear may grant them anoying resistances.
Coding difficulty:  This one could be handled by the monster generation cod=
e.  My experience is that this section of code is pretty straightforward an=
d simple to modify.  Piggy back on the code that creates special monsters f=
or the quests.

4) Earn Bell of Opening (A):  As suggested, maybe your quest nemesis just h=
as the artifact, maybe you need to earn the bell of opening later.  In orde=
r to address why Gehennom, in particular, is boring, attaining the bell mus=
t require that you complete some task while exploring the mazes.

