so that an angel will give you the Bell from 4.  Maybe doing so would be th=
e only way to CHARGE the Bell of Opening, so that you have to rescue at lea=
st one but can rescue more so that you can use the Bell later (in the sanct=
um?).  Maybe some of the lost souls are former crusaders, who reward you wi=
th loot like from 2 above if you rescue them.
Coding difficulty:  Basically piggybacks on the pet code.  Not impossible t=
o alter.

6) Randomized monsters (A, D, E, F):  Not completely random, more that ther=
e is a set of attacks, resistances, and vulnerabilities that are scrambled =
across a set of monsters, much like item appearances are.  Make the attacks=
 strong, the resistances absolute, and the vulnerabilities deadly.  This cr=
eates a new type of identification game, where the player has to determine =
which monsters have which attacks and resistances, maybe with the knowledge=
 that they're going to genocide the ones with the int-draining attack, once=
 they know what they look like.  You could add a "scroll of demonology[1]" =
that works like "identify" but for monsters.  You could make the randomized=
 monsters especially frequent and aggressive after you get the amulet.
